# Repository Instructions

## Rust workflow

- Use the toolchain declared in `rust-toolchain.toml`.
- Run `just verify` before handing off a completed change.
- Run the narrowest relevant test during iteration; use `cargo nextest run <filter>` when possible.
- Treat Clippy warnings as errors and keep code formatted with rustfmt.
- Run `just coverage` when changing behavior whose test coverage is not obvious.

## Project context

- Document supported feature combinations and remove `--all-features` from the `justfile` if features are mutually exclusive.
- Document required services, fixtures, generated files, and whether tests may use the network.
- Document the unsafe-code policy and any platform or MSRV requirements.
- Explain when `Cargo.lock` changes are expected.

## Version control

- This repository uses jj. Do not use Git for history operations.
